      ":question/problem": "![](images/a6/a6f83d3c86e6d5c2e470f68e2e75f32c2fb7573a08cc188d2fd7080103351076.png)\n\nA box with no lid and a square base has a manufacturing cost that depends on two materials. The material for the base costs $$3$ per square meter, and the material for the lateral faces costs $$2$ per square meter. The box must have a volume of $6m^{3}$.\n\nWhat is the value of $x$ for the box that has the smallest production cost?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
